The policy `CanApproveRefunds` combines two requirements: `MinimumTenure(90)` and a role requirement. This handler covers the first.

```csharp
protected override Task HandleRequirementAsync(
    AuthorizationHandlerContext context, MinimumTenure requirement)
{
    var hired = context.User.FindFirstValue("hired_on");

    if (hired is null)
    {
        context.Fail();
        return Task.CompletedTask;
    }

    if (DateTime.Parse(hired) <= DateTime.UtcNow.AddDays(-requirement.Days))
        context.Succeed(requirement);
    else
        context.Fail();

    return Task.CompletedTask;
}
```

A second handler for `MinimumTenure` exists to grant an exemption to agents with a `tenure_waiver` claim. Waived agents are still denied. Why?

